module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Finite
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.Colimits
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.LocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.GlobalSectionsClosed.LocalAgreement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.LocallySurjectiveUnivLE
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Global sections of an étale inverse image come, locally, from the base

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes and `F` a sheaf of sets on the small étale site of `X`.
A global section `t` of the inverse image `i^{-1}F` is a section of the sheafification of a left
Kan extension, so it is described by two local statements, and this file extracts both.

Sheafification is locally surjective, so `t` agrees, on a covering family `V j` of the final
object of the small étale site of `Z`, with a section of the left Kan extension itself. The left
Kan extension at `V j` is a colimit over the objects of the small étale site of `X` equipped with
a morphism `V j ⟶ W ×_X Z`, so each of those sections is the image of a section `s j` of `F` over
such a `W j`. Together: *a global section of `i^{-1}F` is, on a covering of `Z`, pulled back from
sections of `F` over objects of the small étale site of `X`.*

The geometric consequence is the one hypothesis (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 09ZF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZF) is designed to exploit. Each `W j`
has open image in `X`, each point of `Z` is hit by one of the `V j`, and a morphism
`V j ⟶ W j ×_X Z` carries a point of `V j` to a point of `W j` over the same point of `X`. So the
images of the
`W j` form an open subscheme of `X` containing the image of `i`, and hypothesis (1) forces it to be
all of `X` by `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.eq_top_of_zariskiGlobalSectionsMap_surjective`: the family
`W j` covers `X`.

Finally the two identifications of global sections with sections over a final object are
isomorphisms, so surjectivity of the comparison map of Tag 09ZF is equivalent to surjectivity of
the presheaf-level pullback `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleGlobalSectionPullback`. Combined
with the injectivity half, already available as
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.injective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_of_zariskiSurjective`, this
reduces the bijectivity half of Tag 09ZF to the single statement that that pullback is surjective.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isLocallySurjective_smallEtaleToPlus` and
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isLocallySurjective_smallEtaleToSheafify` — the plus construction and
  sheafification on the small étale site are locally surjective at the coefficient universe of
  étale cohomology.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.exists_rep_lan_smallEtaleBaseChange` — a section of the left Kan
  extension along base change is the pullback of a section of `F`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.exists_smallEtaleCover_lift_of_inverseImageSection` — a global section
  of `i^{-1}F` is, on a covering family of `Z`, pulled back from sections of `F`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.mem_smallEtaleImage_of_hom_baseChange` — a morphism into a base change
  puts the images of its points inside the image of the object being base changed.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.iSup_smallEtaleImage_eq_top_of_zariski` — under hypothesis (1), such a
  family of objects of the small étale site of `X` covers `X`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.exists_smallEtaleCover_covering_of_inverseImageSection` — the two
  previous results together: the étale family producing `t` covers `X`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.surjective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_iff` — the comparison map of
  Tag 09ZF is surjective exactly when the presheaf-level pullback is.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isIso_globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison_of_surjective` —
  the bijectivity half of Tag 09ZF, reduced to surjectivity of the presheaf-level pullback.

## Implementation notes

Local surjectivity of the plus construction and of sheafification are not available from
Mathlib here, exactly as local injectivity was not in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EtaleCohomology/GlobalSectionsClosed/LocalAgreement.lean`:
Mathlib's instances constrain the coefficient category to the universe generated by the site,
while étale cohomology is written with coefficients in `Type (max (u + 1) v)` for a free `v`.
The statements under the weaker hypothesis `UnivLE.{max z w, v}` are
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallySurjective_toPlus` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify`, and the two instances below apply them to
the small étale topology, whose objects lie in `Type (u + 1)` and morphisms in `Type u`, so that
the hypothesis needed is `UnivLE.{u + 1, max (u + 1) v}`. Both are global instances on a widely
used construction; both classes are `Prop`-valued, so no instance diamond can arise from them.

The index type of the covering family is the object universe `Type (u + 1)` of the small étale
site, because it is produced by `CategoryTheory.Sieve.exists_eq_ofArrows`.

`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.isIso_globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison_of_surjective`
carries `IsClosedImmersion i`, `CompactSpace X` and `QuasiSeparatedSpace X` although its proof
uses none of them: they are the hypotheses of Tag 09ZF, and recording them here keeps the
reduction aligned with the statement it is a reduction of. Their role in the source is in the two
steps this file does not reach, described below.

What remains of the surjectivity half is the step the source carries out with two external
results. After shrinking each `W j` so that `V j ⟶ W j ×_X Z` is surjective — a closed-immersion
computation on the open image of `V j` — one needs a finite surjective `X' ⟶ X` which factors
Zariski-locally through the covering family `W j`
([Stacks, Tag 09Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09Z0), More on Morphisms 37.45.7, where
quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X` enter), pulls `t` back to `X'`, applies
hypothesis (2) along the finite morphism `X' ⟶ X` to produce a section over `X'`, and descends it
to `X` using descent of sections of an étale sheaf of sets along a surjective integral morphism
([Stacks, Tag 09Z3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09Z3), Remark 59.55.6). Both are
available: Tag 09Z0 is
`Stacks.MoreMorphisms.exists_isFinite_finitePresentation_surjective_zariskiLocallyFactors`, and
Tag 09Z3 is
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.globalSectionsPullback_isEqualizer_of_isFinite_surjective`.  That route
is carried out in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EtaleCohomology/GlobalSectionsClosed/FiniteSurjectiveDescent.lean`
so the reduction in this file is a reduction and no longer a gap.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09ZF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.Plus
open TopologicalSpace

universe u v

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology

section Sheafify

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **The plus construction on the small étale site is locally surjective.** A section of the
plus construction over an object of the small étale site of `Z` is represented by a compatible
family on a covering sieve, so it is locally in the image of the unit.

This is `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_toPlus` at the coefficient universe of étale
cohomology, where Mathlib's instance does not apply. -/
@[sga "3 IV 4.3.11" "(i), special case"]
public instance isLocallySurjective_smallEtaleToPlus
    (P : Z.Etaleᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max (u + 1) v)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      ((Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z).toPlus P) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallySurjective_toPlus (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z) P

/-- **Sheafification on the small étale site is locally surjective.** Every section of the
sheafification of a presheaf of sets on the small étale site of `Z` is, on a covering family,
the image of a section of the presheaf.

Sheafification is the twofold plus construction composed with
`CategoryTheory.plusPlusIsoSheafify`, which is an isomorphism. -/
public instance isLocallySurjective_smallEtaleToSheafify
    (P : Z.Etaleᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max (u + 1) v)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z) P) := by
  set J := Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z
  have h1 : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (J.toSheafify P) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify J P
  rw [← toSheafify_plusPlusIsoSheafify_hom J (Type (max (u + 1) v)) P]
  infer_instance

end Sheafify

variable {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X)

/-- **A section of the left Kan extension is a pullback of a section of `F`.** For an object `V`
of the small étale site of `Z`, every section over `V` of the left Kan extension of `F` along
base change is the image, under the unit of the Kan extension followed by restriction, of a
section of `F` over some object `W` of the small étale site of `X` admitting a morphism
`V ⟶ W ×_X Z`.

The left Kan extension is computed pointwise as a colimit over those data, and the maps into a
colimit of sets are jointly surjective. -/
public theorem exists_rep_lan_smallEtaleBaseChange (V : Z.Etale)
    (F : Sheaf (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X) (Type (max (u + 1) v)))
    (t : ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj).obj (op V)) :
    ∃ (W : X.Etale) (k : V ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj W) (s : F.obj.obj (op W)),
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj).map k.op
        (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lanUnit.app F.obj).app (op W) s) = t := by
  have hcolim := Functor.isPointwiseLeftKanExtensionOfIsLeftKanExtension
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lanUnit.app F.obj) (op V)
  obtain ⟨j, y, hy⟩ := Types.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit hcolim t
  exact ⟨j.left.unop, j.hom.unop, y, hy⟩

/-- **A global section of the inverse image is locally pulled back from the base.** For a sheaf
of sets `F` on the small étale site of `X` and a global section `t` of `i^{-1}F`, there is a
family of objects `V j` of the small étale site of `Z` whose images cover `Z`, objects `W j` of
the small étale site of `X` with morphisms `V j ⟶ W j ×_X Z`, and sections `s j` of `F` over
`W j`, such that the restriction of `t` to `V j` is the pullback of `s j`.

Sheafification is locally surjective, which produces the covering family and a section of the
left Kan extension over each member; those are pullbacks of sections of `F` by
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.exists_rep_lan_smallEtaleBaseChange`. -/
public theorem exists_smallEtaleCover_lift_of_inverseImageSection
    (F : Sheaf (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X) (Type (max (u + 1) v)))
    (t : ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F).obj.obj (op (terminal Z.Etale))) :
    ∃ (α : Type (u + 1)) (V : α → Z.Etale) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ terminal Z.Etale)
      (W : α → X.Etale) (k : ∀ j, V j ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (W j))
      (s : ∀ j, F.obj.obj (op (W j))),
      (⋃ j, Set.range (p j).left.base) = Set.univ ∧
      ∀ j, (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
            ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)).app (op (V j))
          (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj).map (k j).op
            (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lanUnit.app F.obj).app (op (W j)) (s j)))
        = ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F).obj.map (p j).op t := by
  have hS : Presheaf.imageSieve (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)) t ∈
      Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z (terminal Z.Etale) :=
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective.imageSieve_mem _
  obtain ⟨α, Y, p, hEq⟩ := (Presheaf.imageSieve (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)) t).exists_eq_ofArrows
  have hcov : ⋃ j, Set.range (p j).left.base = Set.univ :=
    (Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff p).mp (hEq ▸ hS)
  have hmem : ∀ j, ∃ x, (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)).app (op (Y j)) x
      = ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F).obj.map (p j).op t := by
    intro j
    have hin : (Presheaf.imageSieve (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
        ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)) t).arrows (p j) := by
      rw [hEq]
      exact (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).2 ⟨j, 𝟙 _, (Category.id_comp _).symm⟩
    exact hin
  choose x hx using hmem
  choose W k s hks using fun j ↦ exists_rep_lan_smallEtaleBaseChange i (Y j) F (x j)
  exact ⟨α, Y, p, W, k, s, hcov, fun j ↦ by rw [hks j, hx j]⟩

/-- **A morphism into a base change lands over the image of the object base changed.** If `V` is
an object of the small étale site of `Z` with a morphism to the base change along `i` of an
object `W` of the small étale site of `X`, then the image in `X` of every point of `V` lies in
the open image of `W`.

The morphism carries a point of `V` into `W ×_X Z`, and the two projections of the fibre product
agree in `X`. -/
public theorem mem_smallEtaleImage_of_hom_baseChange {V : Z.Etale} {W : X.Etale}
    (k : V ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj W) (v : V.left) :
    i.base ((V.hom : V.left ⟶ Z).base v) ∈ smallEtaleImage W := by
  have hkw : k.left ≫ (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj W).hom :
      ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj W).left ⟶ Z) = (V.hom : V.left ⟶ Z) :=
    MorphismProperty.Over.w k
  have hsnd : (pullback.snd (W.hom : W.left ⟶ X) i).base (k.left.base v)
      = (V.hom : V.left ⟶ Z).base v :=
    (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply k.left _ v).symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun f : V.left ⟶ Z ↦ f.base v) hkw)
  refine ⟨(pullback.fst (W.hom : W.left ⟶ X) i).base (k.left.base v), ?_⟩
  have hcond : (pullback.fst (W.hom : W.left ⟶ X) i ≫ (W.hom : W.left ⟶ X)).base
        (k.left.base v)
      = (pullback.snd (W.hom : W.left ⟶ X) i ≫ i).base (k.left.base v) := by
    rw [pullback.condition]
  exact Eq.trans
    (((Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ (k.left.base v)).symm.trans hcond).trans
      (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ (k.left.base v)))
    (congrArg i.base hsnd)

/-- The image of `i` lies in the union of the images of a family `W j` of the small étale site
of `X` whenever the objects `V j ⟶ W j ×_X Z` have images covering `Z`. -/
private theorem range_subset_iSup_smallEtaleImage
    {α : Type*} (V : α → Z.Etale) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ terminal Z.Etale)
    (W : α → X.Etale) (k : ∀ j, V j ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (W j))
    (hcov : (⋃ j, Set.range (p j).left.base) = Set.univ) :
    Set.range i.base ⊆ ((⨆ j, smallEtaleImage (W j) : X.Opens) : Set X) := by
  rintro x ⟨z, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ := surjective_terminal_hom Z z
  obtain ⟨j, v, hv⟩ : ∃ j, z₀ ∈ Set.range (p j).left.base :=
    Set.mem_iUnion.mp (hcov ▸ Set.mem_univ z₀)
  have hVj : (V j).hom.base v = z := by
    have hw : (p j).left ≫ ((terminal Z.Etale).hom : (terminal Z.Etale).left ⟶ Z) =
        ((V j).hom : (V j).left ⟶ Z) := MorphismProperty.Over.w (p j)
    calc ((V j).hom : (V j).left ⟶ Z).base v
        = ((p j).left ≫ ((terminal Z.Etale).hom :
            (terminal Z.Etale).left ⟶ Z)).base v := by rw [hw]
      _ = ((terminal Z.Etale).hom : (terminal Z.Etale).left ⟶ Z).base ((p j).left.base v) :=
            Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ v
      _ = z := by rw [hv, hz₀]
  exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨j, hVj ▸ mem_smallEtaleImage_of_hom_baseChange i (k j) v⟩

/-- **Under hypothesis (1) of Tag 09ZF, a family receiving a covering of `Z` covers `X`.** Let
`V j` be a family of objects of the small étale site of `Z` whose images cover `Z`, each equipped
with a morphism to the base change along `i` of an object `W j` of the small étale site of `X`.
If restriction of global sections along `i` is surjective for every sheaf of sets on the Zariski
site of `X`, then the images of the `W j` cover `X`.

The images are open and their union contains the image of `i`, so
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.eq_top_of_zariskiGlobalSectionsMap_surjective` applies. -/
public theorem iSup_smallEtaleImage_eq_top_of_zariski
    (hZar : ∀ G : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Type (max (u + 1) v)),
      Function.Surjective (zariskiGlobalSectionsMap.{u, v} i G))
    {α : Type*} (V : α → Z.Etale) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ terminal Z.Etale)
    (W : α → X.Etale) (k : ∀ j, V j ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (W j))
    (hcov : (⋃ j, Set.range (p j).left.base) = Set.univ) :
    (⨆ j, smallEtaleImage (W j)) = ⊤ := by
  exact eq_top_of_zariskiGlobalSectionsMap_surjective.{u, v} i hZar
    (range_subset_iSup_smallEtaleImage i V p W k hcov)

/-- **The étale family producing a global section of the inverse image covers `X`.** Under
hypothesis (1) of Tag 09ZF, a global section `t` of `i^{-1}F` is, on a covering family of `Z`,
pulled back from sections `s j` of `F` over objects `W j` of the small étale site of `X` *whose
images cover `X`*.

This is the state the source reaches before invoking
[Stacks, Tag 09Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09Z0). -/
public theorem exists_smallEtaleCover_covering_of_inverseImageSection
    (hZar : ∀ G : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Type (max (u + 1) v)),
      Function.Surjective (zariskiGlobalSectionsMap.{u, v} i G))
    (F : Sheaf (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X) (Type (max (u + 1) v)))
    (t : ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F).obj.obj (op (terminal Z.Etale))) :
    ∃ (α : Type (u + 1)) (V : α → Z.Etale) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ terminal Z.Etale)
      (W : α → X.Etale) (k : ∀ j, V j ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (W j))
      (s : ∀ j, F.obj.obj (op (W j))),
      (⨆ j, smallEtaleImage (W j)) = ⊤ ∧
      ∀ j, (toSheafify (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
            ((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj)).app (op (V j))
          (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lan.obj F.obj).map (k j).op
            (((smallEtaleBaseChange i).op.lanUnit.app F.obj).app (op (W j)) (s j)))
        = ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F).obj.map (p j).op t := by
  obtain ⟨α, V, p, W, k, s, hcov, ht⟩ :=
    exists_smallEtaleCover_lift_of_inverseImageSection.{u, v} i F t
  exact ⟨α, V, p, W, k, s,
    iSup_smallEtaleImage_eq_top_of_zariski.{u, v} i hZar V p W k hcov, ht⟩

variable (g : terminal Z.Etale ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (terminal X.Etale))
  (F : Sheaf (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X) (Type (max (u + 1) v)))

/-- The comparison map of Tag 09ZF is surjective exactly when the presheaf-level pullback is:
the two maps conjugating them are components of natural isomorphisms. -/
public theorem surjective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_iff :
    Function.Surjective (smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt.{u, v} i g F) ↔
      Function.Surjective (smallEtaleGlobalSectionPullback.{u, v} i g F) := by
  have hX : Function.Bijective ((Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X)
      (Type (max (u + 1) v)) terminalIsTerminal).hom.app F) :=
    (isIso_iff_bijective _).mp inferInstance
  have hZ : Function.Bijective ((Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      (Type (max (u + 1) v)) terminalIsTerminal).inv.app
        ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F)) :=
    (isIso_iff_bijective _).mp inferInstance
  constructor
  · intro h y
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := h (((Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology Z)
      (Type (max (u + 1) v)) terminalIsTerminal).inv.app
        ((smallEtaleInverseImage.{u, v} i).obj F)) y)
    refine ⟨((Sheaf.ΓNatIsoSheafSections (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X)
      (Type (max (u + 1) v)) terminalIsTerminal).hom.app F) s, hZ.1 ?_⟩
    rw [← smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_apply, hs]
  · intro h y
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hZ.2 y
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h c
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hX.2 a
    exact ⟨s, by rw [smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_apply, hs, ha, hc]⟩

/-- **The bijectivity half of Tag 09ZF, reduced to surjectivity of the presheaf-level pullback.**
Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion into a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme such that
restriction of global sections along `i` is bijective for every sheaf of sets on the Zariski site
of `X`. If the presheaf-level pullback of global sections is surjective for every sheaf of sets
on the small étale site of `X`, then the comparison map
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison` is an isomorphism.

The injectivity half is
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.injective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_of_zariskiSurjective`, which
needs only surjectivity of the Zariski restriction maps; surjectivity is transported from the
presheaf level by `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.surjective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_iff`. -/
public theorem isIso_globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison_of_surjective
    {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X]
    (hZar : ∀ G : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) (Type (max (u + 1) v)),
      Function.Bijective (zariskiGlobalSectionsMap.{u, v} i G))
    (hsurj : ∀ (F : Sheaf (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology X) (Type (max (u + 1) v)))
      (g : terminal Z.Etale ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (terminal X.Etale)),
      Function.Surjective (smallEtaleGlobalSectionPullback.{u, v} i g F)) :
    IsIso (globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison.{u, v} i).val :=
  (isIso_globalSectionsSmallEtaleInverseImageComparison_iff.{u, v} i).mpr fun F gg ↦
    ⟨injective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_of_zariskiSurjective.{u, v} i gg F
        fun G ↦ (hZar G).2,
      (surjective_smallEtaleGlobalSectionsMapAt_iff.{u, v} i gg F).mpr (hsurj F gg)⟩

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology


namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology
variable {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X)
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.Plus
open TopologicalSpace

/-- **A family receiving a covering of `Z` covers `X`, when no open but `X` contains `Z`.** Let
`V j` be a family of objects of the small étale site of `Z` whose images cover `Z`, each equipped
with a morphism to the base change along `i` of an object `W j` of the small étale site of `X`.
If the only open of `X` containing the image of `i` is `X` itself, then the images of the `W j`
cover `X`: they are open and their union contains the image of `i`. -/
public theorem iSup_smallEtaleImage_eq_top_of_forall_eq_top
    (hstar : ∀ U : X.Opens, Set.range i.base ⊆ (U : Set X) → U = ⊤)
    {α : Type*} (V : α → Z.Etale) (p : ∀ j, V j ⟶ terminal Z.Etale)
    (W : α → X.Etale) (k : ∀ j, V j ⟶ (smallEtaleBaseChange i).obj (W j))
    (hcov : (⋃ j, Set.range (p j).left.base) = Set.univ) :
    (⨆ j, smallEtaleImage (W j)) = ⊤ := by
  exact hstar _ (range_subset_iSup_smallEtaleImage i V p W k hcov)

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology

